Description: EAP TLS 1.2 plus automatic Wi-Fi recovery
 Lets the legacy iOS 5/6/7 EAP client negotiate TLS 1.2 (raise-only
 version ceiling) so WPA2-Enterprise networks such as ANU-Secure work.
 .
 Also installs a watchdog: if the device stays "connected" with no
 traffic, it restarts wifid after three failed probes so the link
 re-associates and re-authenticates automatically. Recovery log:
 /var/mobile/Media/wifi-watchdog.log
 .
 1.4.1 handles the iOS 7 EAP context (kTLSProtocol1 with min=max
 TLS 1.0), installs the helper to /usr/bin and ships parent dirs.
